   379	## Amendment — 2026-04-24 — `source_asof` population semantics + `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning
   380	
   381	### Why
   382	
   383	The 2026-04-24 Claim Anatomy Review (`.docs/plans/claim-anatomy-review-2026-04-24.md` §10) identified that `source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>` exists in §4 above as optional metadata but no code path actually populates it. Today's storage path stamps `observed_at = now` (`glean_provider.rs:1182`) regardless of when the underlying source was authored. The Glean/PTY prompts ask for `sourcedAt` per item (`dimension_prompts.rs:608`) but the returned timestamp lives in a JSON blob and is never lifted into the first-class column.
   384	
   385	**Effective behavior today:** every claim freshly synthesized from a 6-month-old Salesforce note looks fresh. Trust Compiler's `freshness_weight` factor (DOS-10) will be calibrated against ingestion time, not evidence time. Stale evidence appears as fresh claims — load-bearing bug present today, that worsens when Trust Compiler ships unless fixed.
   386	
   387	This amendment closes the gap before Trust Compiler ships in v1.4.0 spine (DOS-5).
   388	
   389	### A. Population semantics
   390	
   391	`source_asof` is amended from "optional metadata" to **must-be-populated-when-knowable**, with an explicit population chain:
   392	
   393	```text
   394	populate(source_asof) = pick first available:
   395	  1. LLM-returned `sourcedAt` from `itemSource.sourcedAt` (per dimension_prompts.rs:608 contract)
   396	  2. Glean document `lastModified` / `createdAt` from cited downstream documents
   397	  3. Source-class inference (e.g., for an email source attribution, the email's `Date:` header)
   398	  4. None
   399	```
   400	
   401	If all four fail, `source_asof = None` AND the Provenance envelope emits a new warning variant:
   402	
   403	```rust
   404	pub enum ProvenanceWarning {
   405	    // ...existing variants...
   406	    SourceTimestampUnknown {
   407	        source_index: usize,
   408	        fallback: SourceTimestampFallback,
   409	    },
   410	}
   411	
   412	pub enum SourceTimestampFallback {
   413	    /// Fell back to ingestion time `observed_at` for freshness calculation.
   414	    ObservedAt,
   415	    /// Fell back to claim creation time (worst case — neither source nor ingestion timestamp).
   416	    ClaimCreatedAt,
   417	}
   418	```
   419	
   420	Surfaces (per ADR-0108) render `SourceTimestampUnknown` so the system can see when freshness is being approximated rather than measured.
   421	
   422	### B. Freshness fallback chain (informs DOS-10)
   423	
   424	The freshness factor uses an explicit fallback chain — **conservative on unknown**:
   425	
   426	```text
   427	freshness_input_age = match (source_asof, observed_at):
   428	  (Some(t), _)            => now - t                        // measured evidence age
   429	  (None, Some(t))         => (now - t) + STALENESS_PADDING  // ingestion time + penalty
   430	  (None, None)            => MAX_AGE                        // treat as fully decayed
   431	```
   432	
   433	The `STALENESS_PADDING` (default 30 days, configurable in `config/scoring.toml`) ensures unknown timestamps are treated as old, not fresh. This prevents the system from claiming freshness it can't substantiate. DOS-10's freshness decay table consumes this corrected input.
   434	
   435	### C. `ProvenanceBuilder` enforcement
   436	
   437	The builder lifts `itemSource.sourcedAt` (when present in LLM output) and Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` automatically. Authors do not manually populate the field. The builder emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` when the population chain falls to step 4.
   438	
   439	### D. Consumer issues affected
   440	
   441	| Issue | What changes |
   442	|---|---|
   443	| DOS-211 (Provenance Builder, spine) | Builder lifts `sourcedAt` from `itemSource` JSON or Glean document metadata into `source_asof`. Emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning on full fallback. |
   444	| DOS-5 (Trust Compiler, spine) | `freshness_weight` factor uses the fallback chain in §B above. Conservative on unknown. |
   445	| DOS-10 (Freshness decay table, v1.4.1) | Spec amended to consume the corrected input from this fallback chain. |
   446	| DOS-218 / DOS-219 (pilot abilities, spine) | Acceptance criteria include: produces ≥1 claim with `source_asof` populated and ≥1 claim with `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning, demonstrating the chain works both ways. |
   447	| `glean_provider.rs:1182` write path | Lift Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` before writing SignalEvent / claim row. Don't stamp `observed_at = now` as the only timestamp. |
